From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: never fail a sta_state down transition

mac80211 documents that .sta_state "must not fail for down transitions":
the station is torn down whatever the driver returns, and a non-zero
return only trips WARN_ON_ONCE() in __sta_info_destroy_part2() (NONE ->
NOTEXIST) or the "Driver is not allowed to fail" WARN_ONCE() in
_sta_info_move_state().

ath11k propagates WMI errors from ath11k_mac_station_remove() and
ath11k_station_disassoc(). When a station is deleted while the firmware
is dead (-ESHUTDOWN while ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH is set) or wedged
(-ENOBUFS, CE ring not serviced), the first such deletion after
mac80211 is loaded produces (both WARNs are one-shot):

  WARNING: ... at net/mac80211/sta_info.c:1559 sta_set_sinfo+0x1104/0x1128 [mac80211]
  x0 : 00000000ffffff94    (-ESHUTDOWN; -ENOBUFS = ffffff97 on a zombie QCN6122)
   sta_info_destroy_addr_bss / ieee80211_del_station / nl80211_del_station

(sta_set_sinfo is kallsyms' nearest global symbol in the stripped module;
the PC is in __sta_info_destroy_part2() at the drv_sta_state() check.)

The host-side peer is already freed in the NONE -> NOTEXIST branch when
the firmware delete fails, so report success for all down transitions
and keep the ath11k_warn() lines.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -9932,6 +9932,16 @@
 				    sta->addr);
 	}
 
+	/* mac80211 does not allow a driver to fail a transition down the
+	 * state list: the station is torn down regardless, and an error only
+	 * trips a WARN in _sta_info_move_state()/__sta_info_destroy_part2().
+	 * That happens whenever WMI is unusable - -ESHUTDOWN after a firmware
+	 * crash, -ENOBUFS when the firmware stops servicing its rings - and
+	 * the host-side peer is freed in the NONE -> NOTEXIST branch anyway.
+	 */
+	if (new_state < old_state)
+		ret = 0;
+
 	mutex_unlock(&ar->conf_mutex);
 	return ret;
 }
